notes={
357671:('PARK_FULL_SCOPE_GAP','Limit-permuton forcing. Positive-coefficient arguments do not transfer through cancellation. Need a classification of signed vanishing covers for all pattern sizes, or a genuinely forcing combination with at most five nonzero terms.'),
360520:('PARK_FULL_SCOPE_GAP','Need one exponent depending only on H for all s. Pruning small degree does not remove induced four-cycles. Need a density-preserving induced selection lemma with polynomial loss.'),
360537:('PARK_SUSTAINED_GAP','Primary Definition 5, Conjecture 1, Propositions 1/2, Theorem 2 proof and Appendix B reviewed. Finite-size bootstrapping deteriorates; positive term addition changes the ground space; semiclassical substitution is not an operator bound. Both k=2 and k=3 required. See ATTEMPTS.md.'),
354217:('PARK_ASYMPTOTIC','Probability tending to one at a random hitting time is the endpoint. Choosing covering triples need not give an STS: chosen triples can overlap on pairs. No uniform stopping-time absorption mechanism obtained.'),
354997:('PARK_SUSTAINED_GAP','Definitions 4.1/4.2 and Theorem 4.3/Conjecture 4.4 reviewed. Convex hull insertion, triangulation and dimension induction fail to prove both sentences. Source already proves transfinite growth and dimension-four quasi-pyramidal growth. See ATTEMPTS.md.'),
349500:('PARK_FULL_SCOPE_GAP','Pigeonholing block choices loses exponentially in the number of blocks, not polylogarithmically in dimension. Need a dimension-controlled common incidence rectangle for arbitrary nonparallel blocks.'),
349535:('PARK_FULL_SCOPE_GAP','A narrow direction or cylinder does not supply a whole orthonormal basis. Successive projections need not preserve transitivity. Need simultaneous orthogonal direction selection.'),
349735:('PARK_ASYMPTOTIC','Balanced blow-ups give only the lower bound on extremal induced density. Need a matching upper bound for every k>=4, beyond source k=5. No full route.'),
351513:('PARK_INFINITE','Requires hereditary extraction inside every density-recurrent subset of integers. Finite tests do not prove recurrence for all colorings/density sets. Literal omitted nonzero conventions are a possible domain issue, not significant credit.'),
352789:('PARK_CONTINUUM','Finite sampled pattern, continuum stochastic object. Need a positive-probability path event for every pattern at every interior parameter. Current source has September 2026 v4 and PLMS 2023 record; these bodies remain unread. No present open-status assertion.'),
353124:('PARK_ASYMPTOTIC','Turan density is a limiting extremal quantity. Suspension/blow-up does not automatically realize the exact normalized density with one forbidden p-graph. Need that single-forbidden-graph lifting theorem.'),
345557:('PARK_ANALYTIC','Hausdorff dimension of infinite Diophantine fractal powers. Product dimension inequalities alone do not give the proposed equality. No multivariate construction and matching upper bound; empty/singleton digit-set defects receive zero.'),
348040:('KNOWN_PUBLIC_PROOF','Shankar arXiv:2404.01783v1 Theorem 6 proves stronger ultra-synchronisation for n>=5. Binomial normalization implies Dey Definition 4; small n are routine classical rows (ATTEMPTS.md). Published Discrete Mathematics 348 (2025),114521. Related 348041 already excluded in r198. Zero for a complete public-theorem bridge, not shortness.'),
348995:('PARK_FULL_SCOPE_GAP','Connectivity routes one pair, not arbitrary disjoint pairs. Removing a routed path need not leave a simple polytope graph. Cartesian products of cliques are a subclass. No universal mechanism.'),
341684:('PARK_ASYMPTOTIC','Requires matching and Hamiltonicity thresholds to coincide for all alpha in (0,1/2). Separated constants do not give a common threshold; one finite obstruction does not refute an a.a.s. statement.'),
342197:('PARK_INFINITE','Every admissible fixed down-gap must recur infinitely often. Fibonacci scaling changes the additive gap. Need a recurrence-preserving transformation with unchanged m and unbounded inputs; none obtained. Does not revive 319471.'),
343103:('KNOWN_PUBLIC_PROOF','Ahlbach-David-Oh-Wu arXiv:2009.02644v2 Theorem 1.0.4 proves stab(T)<=r for weakly decreasing row sizes. Persistence gives stabilization at r. Definition 1.0.1, examples/figure text, rectangular flips, Lemma 4.0.2 and final Greene proof reviewed; v1/v2 retained. Public in 2020/2021.'),
339877:('PARK_SUSTAINED_GAP','Source Lemma 7, Theorem 8, Corollaries 10/11 and Conjecture 12 reviewed. Unit exponent case already uniform. Central lifting needs an identity-obstruction balance; character positivity unavailable in general. Nonidentity-fiber counterexamples do not refute this identity claim. ATTEMPTS.md.'),
341405:('PARK_ANALYTIC','Infinite-dimensional Hartree-Fock minimisation at all densities and temperatures. Exchange contributes a negative quadratic term, so radial monotonicity alone is not strict convexity. No global uniqueness mechanism including T=0.'),
336022:('DOMAIN_DEFECT_NO_CREDIT_INTENDED_GAP','Read all four source pages. Epsilon>1 makes the norm bound negative, a zero-credit domain correction. Corpus refuted reference misroutes Wigderson constant-size sampling to Zhao Conjecture 3. The affine construction proves a lower bound, not a refutation of the intended doubly logarithmic upper bound for 0<epsilon<1.')}
